ration the main tracking deployment requires, and — if server-side delegation is needed — the tracking-server configuration surface that must change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written design decision identifies the routing mechanism (gateway-level routing only, or routing requiring a tracking-server configuration change) with rationale grounded in the operator's existing routing and chart patterns.\n- The design specifies the HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance and the configuration the main tracking deployment needs so that artifact traffic reaches the dedicated instance.\n- If server-side delegation is required, the design specifies the tracking-server configuration surface that must change, with no change in meaning to any existing CLI argument or configuration key.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1, de-risking): resolves how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, and whether server-side delegation work exists.\n- HLR-5 (P1, de-risking): the selected design shapes the HTTPRoute created for the dedicated artifacts-only instance's ingress.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":83481,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a59a5dd3308e877f","agent_id":"ab656e2c2f20f84c9","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"c41cca99-0f62-4467-994c-3d051d78910a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:36:17.509Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
