{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8d1e79a0-a1c2-4a98-a030-47a79d5b423f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97d84a1bfd917313","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-8rtkmk24/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E004.md","content":"# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n\n## Description\n\nVerifies and, where needed, extends the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so that workspace resolution — experiment-to-workspace mapping via the workspace provider registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` — functions correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin currently provides this mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations; this work makes the same resolution available to the artifacts-only proxy. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged — authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure without prescribing Kubernetes API mechanics.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context, per the validated assessment of its initialization dependencies (whether workspace store initialization is coupled to tracking store availability).\n- If workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor it into an independent initialization path within the plugin, so the artifacts-only server can initialize only the workspace provider it needs.\n- Ensure workspace resolution can be driven from artifact request paths (experiment/run identity resolvable from the S3 artifact store layout `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) without tracking store availability.\n- Keep the plugin's behavior for the fully-initialized tracking server unchanged — no regression to workspace resolution for non-artifact operations (tracking, model registry, prompt registry).\n- Automated tests covering workspace resolution in both initialization contexts (full server and artifacts-only).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace resolution returns the correct workspace assignment for an experiment in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by automated tests.\n- Existing workspace resolution behavior for the fully-initialized tracking server is unchanged (the plugin's existing test suite passes).\n- If refactoring was required, the independent initialization path is landed with automated tests demonstrating that the plugin initializes workspace resolution without tracking store availability.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — covered.\n- HLR-2 (P0, support): provides the resolution capability that the server-side HTTP 403 enforcement builds on.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":85415,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a59a5dd3308e877f","agent_id":"ab656e2c2f20f84c9","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"2d522f25-3816-43fa-bc27-8eb3c57ab7b2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:36:38.452Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
