{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-987e356c-cf11-47ac-96b5-11cc0ee367e3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83fc0b3290dd1b50","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-8rtkmk24/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E005.md","content":"# Dedicated artifacts-only instance deployment in the MLflow operator\n\n## Description\n\nExtends the MLflow operator's Helm-in-operator pattern to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, distinct from the main tracking Deployment, and to propagate workspace configuration to it using the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment. This is the split-server topology's deployment half: the main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. Gateway API HTTPRoute resources are created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, with the instance's ingress shape following the selected routing design for the split-server topology.\n- Convert the relevant MLflow CR spec fields to Helm values for the artifacts-only instance; the split topology stays declarative — users configure a single MLflow CR rather than managing individual resources.\n- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment, so its container command runs `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication at the ingress level is unchanged).\n- Operator validation that rejects configurations where the artifacts-only instance is enabled without the workspace flags — misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation.\n- Verify that the embedded chart architecture supports the second Deployment without structural changes (per the strategy's assumption) and make any needed structural adjustments within this work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciliation creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n- A CR requesting the artifacts-only instance without the workspace flags is rejected with a clear validation error.\n- Existing single-Deployment reconciliations are unchanged when split-server serving is not enabled.\n- HTTPRoute creation follows the operator's conditional runtime CRD discovery — no HTTPRoute resource is created when Gateway API CRDs are absent.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — covered.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":86065,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a59a5dd3308e877f","agent_id":"ab656e2c2f20f84c9","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"e2e25ac6-5cdc-4e88-a788-d507e6aed55f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22