{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f1d8b9316fa608d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Design artifact traffic routing for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Design artifact traffic routing for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to a dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology: purely through Gateway API HTTPRoute configuration, or through a tracking-server configuration change that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated instance. The answer selects between the two conditional routing implementation branches and determines whether any server-side configuration work exists at all. This investigation resolves the strategy's open question on artifact traffic routing, whose owner is the MLflow Team.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Evaluate routing options for directing artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, consistent with the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply) and its conditional Gateway API HTTPRoute creation via runtime CRD discovery.\n34\t- Determine whether gateway-level routing alone can split artifact traffic while preserving workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance, or whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations.\n35\t- Define the HTTPRoute design for the artifacts-only instance's ingress under the selected option (host/path shape, relationship to the main tracking deployment's route).\n36\t- Deliver a written design decision identifying the selected routing mechanism, the HTTPRoute resources needed, the configuration the main tracking deployment requires, and — if server-side delegation is needed — the tracking-server configuration surface that must change.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A written design decision identifies the routing mechanism (gateway-level routing only, or routing requiring a tracking-server configuration change) with rationale grounded in the operator's existing routing and chart patterns.\n41\t- The design specifies the HTTPRoute resources for the artifacts-only instance and the configuration the main tracking deployment needs so that artifact traffic reaches the dedicated instance.\n42\t- If server-side delegation is required, the design specifies the tracking-server configuration surface that must change, with no change in meaning to any existing CLI argument or configuration key.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- HLR-6 (P1, de-risking): resolves how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, and whether server-side delegation work exists.\n47\t- HLR-5 (P1, de-risking): the selected design shapes the HTTPRoute created for the dedicated artifacts-only instance's ingress.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d1bf80649db39f0","agent_id":"a73ce269f972ab2b3","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"e9b247e1-b3c9-450a-a46b-d6ad5e4ed63a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:39:46.640Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f1d8b9316fa608d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source"