{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aabf063a1b427ba3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If workspace store initialization is coupled to tracking store\n15\t    availability, scope expands from verification to refactoring workspace resolution\n16\t    into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 0\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Artifacts-only workspace resolution in mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tVerifies and, where needed, extends the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so that workspace resolution — experiment-to-workspace mapping via the workspace provider registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` — functions correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin currently provides this mapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations; this work makes the same resolution available to the artifacts-only proxy. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged — authorization reuses the existing auth plugin infrastructure without prescribing Kubernetes API mechanics.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Verify the plugin's workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context, per the validated assessment of its initialization dependencies (whether workspace store initialization is coupled to tracking store availability).\n43\t- If workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor it into an independent initialization path within the plugin, so the artifacts-only server can initialize only the workspace provider it needs.\n44\t- Ensure workspace resolution can be driven from artifact request paths (experiment/run identity resolvable from the S3 artifact store layout `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) without tracking store availability.\n45\t- Keep the plugin's behavior for the fully-initialized tracking server unchanged — no regression to workspace resolution for non-artifact operations (tracking, model registry, prompt registry).\n46\t- Automated tests covering workspace resolution in both initialization contexts (full server and artifacts-only).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Workspace resolution returns the correct workspace assignment for an experiment in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are not initialized, demonstrated by automated tests.\n51\t- Existing workspace resolution behavior for the fully-initialized tracking server is unchanged (the plugin's existing test suite passes).\n52\t- If refactoring was required, the independent initialization path is landed with automated tests demonstrating that the plugin initializes workspace resolution without tracking store availability.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — covered.\n57\t- HLR-2 (P0, support): provides the resolution capability that the server-side HTTP 403 enforcement builds on.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d1bf80649db39f0","agent_id":"a73ce269f972ab2b3","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"242706cd-1006-40dc-8096-84bb18c93af7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:39:47.776Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aabf063a1b427ba3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
