{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd0013ff9f4fec5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Gateway-level artifact traffic routing\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If gateway-level routing alone cannot split artifact traffic,\n17\t    this branch is replaced by the delegation-based routing branch (operator delegation\n18\t    wiring plus tracking-server delegation configuration).\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 8\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Gateway-level artifact traffic routing\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tImplements routing of artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance purely through Gateway API HTTPRoute configuration — no tracking-server configuration change. This branch applies when the routing design for the split-server topology concludes that gateway-level routing suffices to split artifact traffic while preserving workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- HTTPRoute rules (or equivalent Gateway API configuration) that direct artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance's Service while all other traffic continues to reach the main tracking deployment, per the selected routing design.\n44\t- Any updates to the main tracking Deployment's rendered configuration needed to point artifact operations at the dedicated instance, within the operator's Helm values conversion — configuration references only, no server code change.\n45\t- Operator templates and reconciliation for the routing configuration, following the conditional CRD discovery pattern for Gateway API resources.\n46\t- End-to-end verification that routed artifact requests are subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Artifact requests that previously reached the main tracking deployment's artifact endpoints are routed to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, verified end-to-end in a cluster with Gateway API CRDs present.\n51\t- Non-artifact traffic (experiment tracking, model registry, prompt registry) continues to reach the main tracking deployment.\n52\t- Routed artifact requests are subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance — requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — covered via gateway-level routing.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d1bf80649db39f0","agent_id":"a73ce269f972ab2b3","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"78023b8f-76dc-4785-84fd-d4c2b7a1b73b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:39:51.339Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd0013ff9f4fec5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
