 instance, per the selected routing design.\n44\t- HTTPRoute resources consistent with the delegation-based design, following the operator's conditional CRD discovery pattern for Gateway API resources.\n45\t- Reconciliation and validation for the delegation configuration, including rejection of incomplete split-server configurations.\n46\t- End-to-end verification that delegated artifact requests are subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- The main tracking deployment's rendered configuration delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design.\n51\t- Artifact requests reaching the main tracking deployment's artifact endpoints are served via the dedicated artifacts-only instance, verified end-to-end.\n52\t- Non-artifact traffic (experiment tracking, model registry, prompt registry) continues to reach the main tracking deployment.\n53\t- Delegated artifact requests are subject to workspace validation on the artifacts-only instance — requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — covered via delegation wiring (operator side).\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d1bf80649db39f0","agent_id":"a73ce269f972ab2b3","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"4f96fabd-c058-4d87-9a0d-c37cba8d6166","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:39:51.884Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3cb42e7d7f0560a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
