ng on the server's existing artifact serving configuration.\n43\t- Fail-safe behavior when the delegation target is unreachable or unconfigured: a clear error rather than silently serving artifacts from the tracking server.\n44\t- Automated tests covering artifact operations delegated through the configuration, and unchanged artifact serving when the configuration is absent.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- With the delegation configuration set, artifact operations from the tracking server are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n49\t- Without the delegation configuration, the tracking server's artifact serving behaves exactly as today (backwards compatible — no existing configuration key changes meaning).\n50\t- A misconfigured delegation (unreachable or invalid target) produces a clear error rather than silently serving artifacts from the tracking server.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — covered via the server-side delegation configuration.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d1bf80649db39f0","agent_id":"a73ce269f972ab2b3","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"697841c6-37a9-42ae-9159-00b05191f2a9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:39:52.531Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-954c5d649ab072d1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
