{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fecefad3db52a7e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate workspace resolution in the artifacts-only server context\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves whether the existing workspace resolution machinery — the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin (the workspace provider registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and the `kubernetes://` workspace store — can resolve experiment-to-workspace membership in an MLflow server running in `--artifacts-only` mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The answer determines the scope of the plugin and server implementation work that follows: verification only, or refactoring workspace resolution into an initialization path independent of tracking store availability. This investigation resolves the strategy's open question on workspace store initialization coupling, together with the assumptions that the workspace store is queryable without tracking stores and that artifact request paths carry enough information to resolve workspace membership.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Determine whether workspace store initialization in `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` depends on tracking store or model registry store availability, and map the plugin's full initialization dependency chain.\n34\t- Determine whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store provides experiment-to-workspace mapping that is accessible without initializing tracking stores.\n35\t- Validate that artifact request paths — scoped to the S3 artifact store layout `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`, the standard RHOAI configuration — carry sufficient information (experiment ID or run ID) to resolve workspace membership, and document limitations of non-standard artifact roots.\n36\t- Deliver a written assessment with a pass/fail verdict per question and, if coupling is found, a refactoring plan that factors workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, detailed enough to scope the follow-on implementation.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A written assessment states, with code-level references into the plugin and server sources, whether workspace store initialization depends on tracking store availability, and whether the workspace store is queryable without tracking stores.\n41\t- A written verdict states whether artifact request paths in the S3 artifact store layout provide the information needed to resolve workspace membership, including documented edge cases and limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n42\t- If any coupling is found, the assessment contains a concrete refactoring plan for an independent workspace-resolution initialization path, sufficient to estimate the follow-on plugin work.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- HLR-2 (P0, de-risking): establishes that workspace validation of artifact requests is feasible before the server-side enforcement work starts.\n47\t- HLR-7 (P1, de-risking): resolves the strategy's open question of whether plugin workspace resolution functions in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aedc5e6f7f2746b2","agent_i