h\" — that does change the implementation approach. So open_questions 0 for E003 vs -1 for E005 is arguably inconsistent. But is this \"1-2 arguable values\"? This is the sort of borderline thing that costs at most a point under \"1\". Let me weigh: E004 open_questions -1 rationale says \"resolved by the investigation this epic depends on, but the epic's implementation approach is not yet fixed\" — that's actually the -1 condition being applied (\"not fixed\"). E003's rationale claims approach is fully specified. For E003, the flag-combination behavior is well specified, and the rewrite fallback only applies if coupling found — the validation approach (resolve path → look up workspace → delegate to auth plugin) is the same; only the init path it builds on changes (in the plugin, E004's concern). So E003 open_questions 0 is defensible. E005: HTTPRoute design not yet determined — genuinely open. OK, I find these defensible.\n\nInvestigation signals:\n- E001: question_specificity 1 ✓, source_accessibility 1 ✓ (source-determinable), local_runnability 0 — rubric range? Let me check the local_runnability rubric. From the table: signal 3 local_runnability... I saw signals 1-2 and 4-5. Let me check signal 3's range. Let me view the rest.\n\nActually the sed output cut off at signal 2. Signal 3 local_runnability likely has range -1/0/+1. E001 local_runnability 0 with \"full runtime verification cannot happen purely as local libraries\" — plausibly correct.\n\nLet me check line ~207 for signal 3.","signature":"3b80ddd086f946cbb88495baa655b560"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40306,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aedc5e6f7f2746b2","agent_id":"adfa70934f3d680a7","session_id":"b33f4375-e5e7-42e1-a4f6-de864124642b","uuid":"24527f5e-f4a4-48a3-8202-3bdd795f4210","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:46:13.940Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAIS